  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "rVDgSjhh2AA+/rEpg1xnMhjXybk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:33:36.797Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The Flowable card for dxdy has no website link on it. The row nonetheless carries a domain, dxdydigital.com, which means the identity had to be established outside the directory rather than read off the listing.\n\nThat is a small but concrete limit on what a directory sweep produces. Where the vendor's card omits a field, the mined row either stays blank or is completed from another source, and the two cases look identical afterwards. For a sweep that was explicitly not imprint-swept, knowing which fields came from the card and which were resolved elsewhere is the difference between a verified and an assumed record.\n\nThe firm is excluded in any case: its footprint is recorded as US plus Sri Lanka and Singapore, outside the EU scope of this brief.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- dxdy (US + LK/SG) \u2014 dxdydigital.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Non-EU. No website link on the Flowable card \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:33:36.797037Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:33:36.797041Z"
    }
  },
